  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 222 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe latest deterministic GFS and EC solns from this morning are\nindicating a mid level trough impacting the central CONUS \nSaturday. However, with not much in the way of moisture \navailable this weekend, dry conditions are expected to continue \nacross the area. In the wake of the trough Saturday, low \namplitude ridging will develop and persist across the central \nCONUS through Tuesday. This will lead to a dry forecast and \nafter Friday, max temperatures that are near normal (through \nFriday) to above normal (Saturday through Tuesday). Highs \nthrough Friday will be generally in the 50s with highs reaching \ninto the 60s Saturday through Tuesday. Looking at the latest \nNBM, EC and GFS ensembles, there decent agreement in warm \ntemperatures (highs in the 60s) continuing into the middle and \nend of next week.",
